The WARN is triggered because the device's kobj has already been removed from sysfs (kobj->sd is NULL after device_del ran), meaning the port is holding a stale pointer to a usb_device that's been unregistered. The root cause appears to be that the port maintains references to usb2_dev/usb3_dev even after they've been cleaned up.

The deattach path should clear these pointers via typec_partner_deattach, but something's going wrong with the ordering — either the deattach doesn't run or the usb device's sysfs directory is already gone when typec_partner_unlink_device gets called from typec_unregister_partner. I'm trying to recall if there's a known upstream fix for this, possibly involving partner_link_lock or a missing check in the UCSI driver.
